# night lab champion #19: In sealed pockets and walled rooms (the observer's world 16 and world 2: many presses, few doors) the wave leaks through every wall cell alike, so the nearest rock is pressed as often as the door. The harness already teaches the leak per hue (a door that opens raises it, rock that does nothing lowers it); a DOORNESS contrast amplifies a wall cell's leak by how much it exceeds the mean leak of the solid cells around it, so a door or rubble tile in a rock wall becomes the one bright exit, while the knowledge-priced wave (#18, best untuned) is kept.

channel source
channel solid
channel free
channel thing
channel scent
channel bad
channel here
channel leak
channel value
channel dark
channel door
channel injection
channel wave
channel trail

rule track:
  when 0.9454
  set trail = max(here, 0.7833 * trail)

rule darkness:
  when 1.493
  set dark = 0.4482 * (1 - free) * (1 - solid) + 0.5 * avg8(dark)

# a wall cell that gives more than the walls around it stands out: contrast of its taught leak against its solid neighbours' mean
rule doorness:
  when 1
  set door = clamp(leak + 2.026 * (leak - sum8(solid * leak) / (sum8(solid) + 0.01)) * min(1, 0.5 * sum8(solid)), 0, 1)

rule inject:
  when 1
  set injection = max(where(scent + thing < 0.05, 0, source), thing * (0.959 - bad), where(scent + thing < 0.05, source, 0) * (0.3 + 2.43 * dark)) / (1.371 + 0.5 * sum8(solid))

# unknown ground costs extra; walls pass the wave by their CONTRASTED leak, so doors outshine the rock around them
rule plan:
  when 1
  set wave = max(injection, (1 - 0.08 * (1 - free)) * max(0.94 * max4(wave), 0.916214 * max8(wave))) * (1 - solid * (1 - door))

rule read:
  when 1.002
  set value = wave * (1.051 - 0.3434 * trail)
